  "premise": "The order of independent confirmation matters: a trend or momentum event followed within a short window by an independent participation event in the same direction carries directional information, while the reverse order does not. The model is M1.0; MR6 is a research family, not a model version.",
  "economic_rationale": "A trend reading states that the auction has chosen a side. An independent participation reading states that new volume is entering on that side. When participation follows the trend, the later event is evidence that the move is being accepted by a second, non-price family; when participation leads, the trend event is only a lagging description of the same volume. The ordered test separates acceptance from description, and the reverse-order cells are the control that falsifies the order premise if they pass. MR6.5 adds a confirmed level because location is the obvious confound: participation at a level can be absorption rather than acceptance.",
